  "instructions": [
    "Heat 2 tablespoons of sesame oil in a large Dutch oven over medium-high heat.",
    "Add the beef and cook until browned, breaking it up with a spoon as it cooks.",
    "Add the onion and garlic and cook until the onion is translucent.",
    "Add the caraway seed and cook for 1 minute.",
    "Sprinkle the flour over the meat and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly.",
    "Add the beef broth, red wine, tomatoes, carrots, potatoes, thyme, bay leaves, black pepper, salt, and water to the pot.",
    "Stir to combine, then bring the mixture to a boil.",
    "Cover the pot and transfer it to the oven. Braise the stew for 2 hours, or until the meat is tender.",
    "Remove the pot from the oven and stir in the sesame oil.",
    "Serve the stew hot, garnished with fresh herbs if desired.",
    "Serve the stew in a Korean-style brass bowl, garnished with a sprinkle of caraway seed if desired."
  ],
